## Workflow Overview

### Data Collection

Business data is submitted through the frontend application and stored in Supabase.

### Automation Trigger

Database events trigger n8n workflows automatically.

### AI Processing

Data is enriched and analyzed using AI services to generate insights, sentiment scores, and recommendations.

### Storage

Processed results are stored back into Supabase.

### Visualization

The dashboard retrieves analytics and presents them through an intuitive user interface.

---

## Local Setup

### 1. Clone Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/ai-agent-smb.git
cd ai-agent-smb
```

### 2. Install Frontend Dependencies

```bash
cd frontend
npm install
```

### 3. Configure Environment Variables

Create a `.env` file using `.env.example`.

Example:

```env
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=YOUR_SUPABASE_URL
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR_SUPABASE_KEY
OPENAI_API_KEY=YOUR_OPENAI_KEY
```

### 4. Start Frontend

```bash
npm run dev
```

### 5. Start n8n

```bash
docker compose up -d
```

### 6. Open Application

Frontend:

```text
http://localhost:5173
```

n8n:

```text
http://localhost:5678
```

